('693fa53b-08bd-5c62-b281-196ae3d81230'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The anterior colporrhaphy:', '["Repair of rectocele","Repair of uterine prolapse","Vaginal vault suspension","Repair of cystocele","Incontinence procedure"]'::jsonb, 'Repair of cystocele', 'Often performed with Kelly plication for stress incontinence.'),
('58267690-9979-59ed-9c12-232cf2fa984d'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The Manchester operation:', '["TVT and its associated anatomical structures","Amputation of cervix, shortening of cardinal ligaments, and anterior/posterior repair (for uterin","Burch colposuspension and its associated anatomical structures","Sacrocolpopexy and its associated anatomical structures","Hysterectomy and its associated anatomical structures"]'::jsonb, 'Amputation of cervix, shortening of cardinal ligaments, and anterior/posterior repair (for uterin', 'Preserves the uterus (for women who desire fertility).'),
('2220667d-1307-5f3d-bae1-4e6c4746cd8d'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The LeFort colpocleisis:', '["Sacrocolpopexy and its associated structures","Hysterectomy and its associated structures","Partial obliteration of the vagina","Burch procedure and its associated structures","TVT and its associated structures"]'::jsonb, 'Partial obliteration of the vagina', 'Obliterative procedure (high success rate, low morbidity).'),
('1cbe14ff-2a28-583c-b521-8e34607dd302'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The McRoberts maneuver:', '["Forceps delivery","Hyperflexion of maternal thighs","Episiotomy","Vacuum delivery","Delivery of anterior shoulder"]'::jsonb, 'Hyperflexion of maternal thighs', 'Frees the impacted anterior shoulder by rotating the pubic symphysis.'),
('57bdae9e-ec4d-591c-b094-3e7ac4e2cd8f'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The Zavanelli maneuver:', '["C-section","Delivery of posterior arm","Replacement of fetal head into vagina","Vacuum extraction","Episiotomy"]'::jsonb, 'Replacement of fetal head into vagina', 'Last resort for shoulder dystocia (cephalic replacement).'),
('913acb4d-d62c-57e2-81e6-2a02fb9ccfba'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The episiotomy is:', '["Incision of the bladder and its associated anatomical structures","Incision of the cervix and its associated anatomical structures","Incision of the rectum and its associated anatomical structures","Surgical incision of the perineum to enlarge the vaginal outlet during childbirth","Incision of the uterus and its associated anatomical structures"]'::jsonb, 'Surgical incision of the perineum to enlarge the vaginal outlet during childbirth', 'Mediolateral episiotomy (directed to the right) reduces risk of third-degree tear.'),
('358bf6bb-f351-56fb-93fb-8f196129e417'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'A third-degree perineal tear involves:', '["Perineal body, external anal sphincter","Perineal skin, muscles, and rectal mucosa","Only perineal skin","Perineal muscles only","Vaginal wall only"]'::jsonb, 'Perineal body, external anal sphincter', 'Obstetric anal sphincter injury (OASIS) requiring sphincteroplasty.'),
('92625cb3-93e7-5a90-85a4-8d5f410e75ab'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'A fourth-degree perineal tear involves:', '["Perineal body, external and internal sphincters, and rectal mucosa","Only perineal skin and its associated anatomical structures","Vaginal wall only and its associated anatomical structures","Anal sphincter only and its associated anatomical structures","Perineal muscles only and its associated anatomical structures"]'::jsonb, 'Perineal body, external and internal sphincters, and rectal mucosa', 'Complete tear through the anal canal into the rectum.'),
('8d15a9b6-7d86-51ff-ad20-8f6a151dc355'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The obturator internus muscle:', '["Is a hip extensor and its associated anatomical structures","Is a thigh adductor and its associated anatomical structures","Is a hip flexor and its associated anatomical structures","Lines the posterior pelvic wall and its associated anatomical structures","Lines the lateral pelvic wall (originates from obturator membrane and ischium"]'::jsonb, 'Lines the lateral pelvic wall (originates from obturator membrane and ischium', 'Obturator internus tendon exits through the lesser sciatic foramen.'),
('891376ce-767d-5524-93d0-94be9828a238'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The obturator internus is innervated by:', '["Sciatic nerve","Nerve to obturator internus","Femoral nerve","Obturator nerve","Pudendal nerve"]'::jsonb, 'Nerve to obturator internus', 'Nerve runs a recurrent course through the lesser sciatic foramen.'),
('55cc9691-173b-5670-b200-6e6591c14c57'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The piriformis is innervated by:', '["Nerve to piriformis","Pudendal nerve","Sciatic nerve","Obturator nerve","Superior gluteal nerve"]'::jsonb, 'Nerve to piriformis', 'Piriformis is the key muscle dividing the greater sciatic foramen.'),
('0e7fa82d-3c42-5958-88ec-bdbe39e681b7'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The coccygeus (ischiococcygeus) is innervated by:', '["Pudendal nerve","S4-S5 spinal nerves","Inferior gluteal nerve","Sciatic nerve","Obturator nerve"]'::jsonb, 'S4-S5 spinal nerves', 'Coccygeus forms the posterior part of the pelvic diaphragm.'),
('85c8ca7e-928a-5697-8a04-673ed6f06cfa'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The pubococcygeus is innervated by:', '["Pudendal nerve","Obturator nerve","Inferior rectal nerve","Perineal nerve","Nerve to levator ani"]'::jsonb, 'Nerve to levator ani', 'Runs on the superior (pelvic) surface of the levator ani.'),
('4969d421-1136-558e-831b-4dcd9bf983ca'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The iliococcygeus is innervated by:', '["Sciatic nerve","Pudendal nerve","Nerve to levator ani","Obturator nerve","Inferior gluteal nerve"]'::jsonb, 'Nerve to levator ani', 'Iliococcygeus (the lateral part of the levator ani) may be thin or deficient.'),
('899d0e8d-cd9e-595a-8fbb-78fcf237b357'::uuid, 'Anatomy (Paper 2)', 'Pelvis and Perineum', 'The perineal nerve branches supply:', '["Only bulbospongiosus and its associated anatomical structures","Only the urethral sphincter and its associated anatomical structures","Only ischiocavernosus and its associated anatomical structures","The external urethral sphincter, ischiocavernosus, bulbospongiosus, transverse perineal muscles","Only skin and its associated anatomical structures"]'::jsonb, 'The external urethral sphincter, ischiocavernosus, bulbospongiosus, transverse perineal muscles', 'Perineal nerve (terminal branch of pudendal) supplies the urogenital triangle.'),
